.SS "int form_alert (void * ns, const char * fmt,  ...)"
.PP
show a dialog box 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP - the session that caused this dialog, or NULL 
.br
\fIfmt\fP - the message to display. may contain -substitutions as per printf() 
.br
\fI...\fP - variables of appropriate type and number for -substitutions
.RE
.PP

.SS "int form_dial (void * ns, alert_type at, alert_buttons ab, const char * msg, const char * btxt)"
.PP
handle a dialog. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
index of selected button if ab==ALERT_BUTTONS_CUSTOM, or one of { NOIR_SUCC, NOIR_FAIL } otherwise. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP - the session that caused this dialog, or NULL 
.br
\fIat\fP - what symbol to show (ALERT_ERROR/ALERT_QUESTION) 
.br
\fIab\fP - what buttons to show (ALERT_BUTTONS_OK,ALERT_BUTTONS_YES_NO,ALERT_BUTTONS_CUSTOM) 
.br
\fImsg\fP - the message to display 
.br
\fIbtxt\fP - the labels for the buttons if ab==ALERT_BUTTONS_CUSTOM, separated by pipe-characters '|'
.RE
.PP

.SS "void form_file_edit (const char * op, char ** t)"
.PP
user tries to copy or move a file on top of itself. 
.PP
ask them for a better target name. this function will block until the user decides; if after the call the src and tgt names are still the same, the calling function should abort, otherwise, it should copy/move/rename. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIop\fP - the operation in question, single word ('copy' or 'move'), or full description 
.br
\fIt\fP - where the pointer to the target name is stored (may change)
.RE
.PP

.SS "static void form_file_edit_cxl (GtkWindow * win, gpointer data)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
break inner event-loop for 'copy over?'-dialog. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIwin\fP - the window the dialog lives in 
.br
\fIdata\fP - a pointer to a conditional we'll set to 0 to break the loop
.RE
.PP

